    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-95780",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(200,0.52),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(X=109).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ | $\\,0.7454\\,$ | $\\,0.7486\\,$ | $\\,0.7517\\,$ | $\\,0.7549\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ | $\\,0.7794\\,$ | $\\,0.7823\\,$ | $\\,0.7852\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ | $\\,0.8078\\,$ | $\\,0.8106\\,$ | $\\,0.8133\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=200$ and $p=0.52.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =200\\cdot 0.52 \\\\  & =104 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =200\\cdot (1-0.52) \\\\  & =96 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(200)(0.52)=104\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(200)(0.52)(1-0.52)=49.92.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(104,49.92).$\n\nNow, we can approximate the desired probability $P(X=109).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=109)≈P(108.5\\le Y\\le 109.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(108.5\\le Y\\le 109.5) & =P(\\frac{108.5-104}{\\sqrt{49.92}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{109.5-104}{\\sqrt{49.92}}) \\\\  & ≈P(0.64\\le Z\\le 0.78) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.78)-P(Z<0.64) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.78)-P(Z\\le 0.64) \\\\  & =Φ(0.78)-Φ(0.64) \\\\  & =0.7823-0.7389 \\\\  & =0.0434\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=109)≈0.043.\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.0439.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "grade": "Incorrect",
      "source_grade": "Incorrect",
